1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,730
Before dawn on Thursday, April 28, 2011, a

2
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:09,171
parking lot in Los Angeles fills with police cars.

3
00:00:09,621 --> 00:00:12,863
Officers pull on body armor. Helmets. Shields.

4
00:00:13,313 --> 00:00:16,319
More than 1,300 of them, from more than a

5
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:17,419
dozen agencies.

6
00:00:17,419 --> 00:00:20,718
Their target is one neighborhood gang, in the

7
00:00:20,718 --> 00:00:22,551
harbor town of San Pedro.

8
00:00:23,001 --> 00:00:25,632
Officials would call it the largest gang

9
00:00:25,632 --> 00:00:27,737
takedown in Los Angeles history.

10
00:00:28,187 --> 00:00:31,211
How does one street gang hold a port town for

11
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:31,816
40 years?

12
00:00:31,816 --> 00:00:34,035
And why, after all of this, would

13
00:00:34,035 --> 00:00:36,656
investigators be back again, and again?

14
00:00:37,256 --> 00:00:39,752
This is the case of Rancho San Pedro.

15
00:00:42,352 --> 00:00:45,360
San Pedro sits at the bottom of Los Angeles.

16
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:49,225
It's part of the city, about 25 miles south of

17
00:00:49,225 --> 00:00:51,229
downtown, on San Pedro Bay.

18
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:54,674
Next to it is the Port of Los Angeles.

19
00:00:54,674 --> 00:00:58,064
Seven thousand 500 acres of land and water.

20
00:00:58,064 --> 00:00:59,878
43 miles of waterfront.

21
00:00:59,878 --> 00:01:03,346
Every year since 2000, the busiest container

22
00:01:03,346 --> 00:01:05,396
port in the United States.

23
00:01:05,846 --> 00:01:08,333
Container ships wait offshore for their turn

24
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:09,067
at the docks.

25
00:01:09,517 --> 00:01:12,778
In 2016 alone, the port moved almost 8.9

26
00:01:12,778 --> 00:01:14,734
million container units.

27
00:01:14,734 --> 00:01:18,321
The busiest year ever, it said, for any port

28
00:01:18,321 --> 00:01:20,440
in the Western Hemisphere.

29
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:23,355
Away from the docks, San Pedro is a

30
00:01:23,355 --> 00:01:26,383
neighborhood of homes and small businesses.

31
00:01:26,383 --> 00:01:29,271
And since the 1970s, it has also been the

32
00:01:29,271 --> 00:01:31,173
