33
00:01:31,623 --> 00:01:34,908
Its name is Rancho San Pedro. RSP.

34
00:01:35,358 --> 00:01:39,359
By 2011, according to federal agencies, it has

35
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:41,881
about 600 documented members.

36
00:01:41,881 --> 00:01:44,403
And more than 400 associates.

37
00:01:44,853 --> 00:01:47,663
The Los Angeles city attorney at the time,

38
00:01:47,663 --> 00:01:50,272
Carmen Trutanich, grew up in San Pedro.

39
00:01:50,272 --> 00:01:53,216
He remembered the gang from his school days.

40
00:01:53,666 --> 00:01:56,653
Over the decades, he said, it became a cancer.

41
00:01:57,653 --> 00:02:00,214
The case that leads to that April morning

42
00:02:00,214 --> 00:02:01,151
starts quietly.

43
00:02:01,601 --> 00:02:04,630
About two and a half years earlier, the ATF

44
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:07,519
and the Los Angeles Police Department had

45
00:02:07,519 --> 00:02:09,914
started a joint project. The goal:

46
00:02:09,914 --> 00:02:12,097
cut violent crime in San Pedro.

47
00:02:12,547 --> 00:02:15,528
Month after month, informants and undercover

48
00:02:15,528 --> 00:02:18,713
officers do one thing, over and over. They buy.

49
00:02:19,163 --> 00:02:21,870
By the end, they've bought 90 firearms.

50
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:24,509
Short-barreled shotguns. Machine guns.

51
00:02:24,509 --> 00:02:26,036
Assault-style weapons.

52
00:02:26,036 --> 00:02:29,091
The ATF said many were suspected of links to

53
00:02:29,091 --> 00:02:30,619
the gang's activities.

54
00:02:31,069 --> 00:02:31,716
And drugs.

55
00:02:31,716 --> 00:02:35,015
Methamphetamine. Heroin. Cocaine. Crack. Marijuana.

56
00:02:35,465 --> 00:02:36,935
Each sale is evidence.

57
00:02:36,935 --> 00:02:39,940
One federal indictment names three defendants

58
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:43,012
in drug deals, including a sale of more than a

59
00:02:43,012 --> 00:02:44,681
pound of methamphetamine.

60
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:48,134
Its lead defendant, prosecutors alleged,

61
00:02:48,134 --> 00:02:51,361
brokered the sale of 22 firearms, including

62
00:02:51,361 --> 00:02:52,487
assault rifles.

63
00:02:52,487 --> 00:02:55,864
Other charges cover illegal weapon sales, and

64
00:02:55,864 --> 00:02:57,441
immigration offenses.

65
00:02:57,891 --> 00:03:00,567
Investigators also accused the gang of

66
00:03:00,567 --> 00:03:03,737
intimidating witnesses, threatening employees

67
00:03:03,737 --> 00:03:06,203
of a housing project, and targeting

68
00:03:06,203 --> 00:03:08,387
African-Americans in San Pedro.

69
00:03:08,837 --> 00:03:11,799
By the end, the case pulls in the DEA.

70
00:03:11,799 --> 00:03:15,074
Homeland Security Investigations. The IRS.

71
00:03:15,074 --> 00:03:16,555
The Secret Service.

72
00:03:16,555 --> 00:03:18,271
Housing investigators.

73
00:03:18,271 --> 00:03:19,674
State corrections.

74
00:03:20,124 --> 00:03:23,630
By spring 2011, a federal grand jury in Los

75
00:03:23,630 --> 00:03:26,565
Angeles has returned 12 indictments.

76
00:03:26,565 --> 00:03:28,359
Prosecutors are ready.

77
00:03:29,359 --> 00:03:31,684
The operation is called Pirate Town.

78
00:03:32,134 --> 00:03:35,235
Teams roll out of the staging area in the dark.

79
00:03:35,235 --> 00:03:37,874
More than 90 search warrants, across the

80
00:03:37,874 --> 00:03:39,259
harbor area, at once.

81
00:03:39,709 --> 00:03:43,204
At one house after another, the routine is the same.

82
00:03:43,204 --> 00:03:43,943
Shields up.

83
00:03:43,943 --> 00:03:45,421
Lights on the windows.

84
00:03:45,421 --> 00:03:47,773
Officers move in on the front door.

85
00:03:48,223 --> 00:03:50,124
Patrol cars block the street.

86
00:03:50,124 --> 00:03:52,810
Red and blue lights wash over the houses.

87
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:56,076
Suspects are walked out in handcuffs and put

88
00:03:56,076 --> 00:03:57,164
into patrol cars.

89
00:03:57,614 --> 00:04:00,576
By morning, 80 people are in custody.

90
00:04:00,576 --> 00:04:03,938
66 on state weapons and narcotics charges.

91
00:04:03,938 --> 00:04:06,019
14 on federal indictments.

92
00:04:06,469 --> 00:04:09,556
About 230 people are named in federal and

93
00:04:09,556 --> 00:04:11,212
state court documents.

94
00:04:11,212 --> 00:04:13,998
Officers seize 14 more guns that day,

95
00:04:13,998 --> 00:04:15,579
including a silencer.

96
00:04:16,029 --> 00:04:18,589
At a processing center, agents check names

97
00:04:18,589 --> 00:04:20,295
against lists and paperwork.

98
00:04:20,745 --> 00:04:23,863
Claude Arnold, who led ICE's investigators in

99
00:04:23,863 --> 00:04:26,703
Los Angeles, said children were sometimes

100
00:04:26,703 --> 00:04:28,989
present during the gang's crimes.

101
00:04:28,989 --> 00:04:32,107
One arrestee, he said, was a teenager who had

102
00:04:32,107 --> 00:04:34,670
just become an adult, with no record,

103
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:37,510
allegedly persuaded by her mother, a gang

104
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:40,073
member, to transport methamphetamine.

105
00:04:40,523 --> 00:04:42,870
He called the operation a major blow.

106
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:43,856
The U.S.

107
00:04:43,856 --> 00:04:46,802
attorney in Los Angeles, André Birotte, said

108
00:04:46,802 --> 00:04:48,141
the goal was simple.

109
00:04:48,591 --> 00:04:51,738
He said similar sweeps had already hit other

110
00:04:51,738 --> 00:04:53,025
Los Angeles gangs.

111
00:04:53,025 --> 00:04:55,313
The 38th Street gang. Lennox 13.

112
00:04:55,313 --> 00:04:56,386
Armenian Power.

113
00:04:56,386 --> 00:04:59,317
Their leaders, he said, thought they were

114
00:04:59,317 --> 00:05:00,175
untouchable.

115
00:05:00,625 --> 00:05:03,633
And LAPD chief Charlie Beck added a warning.

116
00:05:04,083 --> 00:05:07,360
The federal indictments name 26 defendants.

117
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:10,483
About half face a possible life sentence.

118
00:05:10,483 --> 00:05:13,302
The county district attorney plans to

119
00:05:13,302 --> 00:05:16,350
prosecute about 145 more in state court.

120
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,593
Not everyone is caught.

121
00:05:18,593 --> 00:05:21,946
Weeks later, the ATF offers a $5,000 reward

122
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:25,611
for one of its primary targets, still at large.

123
00:05:26,611 --> 00:05:28,701
The arrests were only half of the plan.

124
00:05:29,151 --> 00:05:32,134
At the same time, the city attorney's office

125
00:05:32,134 --> 00:05:33,490
goes to civil court.

126
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:36,201
It files a gang injunction, and nuisance

127
00:05:36,201 --> 00:05:38,777
abatement suits against five homes and

128
00:05:38,777 --> 00:05:41,624
businesses tied to gang and drug activity.

129
00:05:41,624 --> 00:05:43,658
One of them is a pizza parlor.

130
00:05:44,108 --> 00:05:47,328
In early June, a Superior Court judge grants

131
00:05:47,328 --> 00:05:48,425
the injunction.

132
00:05:48,425 --> 00:05:51,937
The safety zone covers more than 7 square miles.

133
00:05:52,387 --> 00:05:55,263
Inside it, gang members named in the order

134
00:05:55,263 --> 00:05:58,343
can't associate with each other in public, or

135
00:05:58,343 --> 00:05:59,918
carry weapons or drugs.

136
00:06:00,368 --> 00:06:02,694
The idea is pressure from every side.

137
00:06:02,694 --> 00:06:04,140
Prison for the leaders.

138
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,843
And for everyone else, a neighborhood where

139
00:06:06,843 --> 00:06:08,667
the gang can't openly gather.

140
00:06:09,667 --> 00:06:12,605
But Rancho San Pedro doesn't answer only to

141
00:06:12,605 --> 00:06:13,699
its own leaders.

142
00:06:14,149 --> 00:06:17,576
Federal prosecutors say it operates under the

143
00:06:17,576 --> 00:06:20,395
control of the Mexican Mafia. La Eme.

144
00:06:20,395 --> 00:06:23,366
A prison gang that, according to Police

145
00:06:23,366 --> 00:06:26,336
Magazine, was founded in 1957, inside a

146
00:06:26,336 --> 00:06:28,165
California youth prison.

147
00:06:28,615 --> 00:06:31,008
Its leaders are in state prisons.

148
00:06:31,008 --> 00:06:32,894
But street gangs pay them.

149
00:06:32,894 --> 00:06:34,780
Prosecutors call it a tax.

150
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:37,609
A cut of drug sales, sent up to the men

151
00:06:37,609 --> 00:06:40,873
inside, in exchange for protection, according

152
00:06:40,873 --> 00:06:41,671
to the FBI.

153
00:06:42,121 --> 00:06:45,272
In other Los Angeles cases, prosecutors have

154
00:06:45,272 --> 00:06:48,422
described go-betweens they call secretaries.

155
00:06:48,422 --> 00:06:51,502
People with ordinary jobs who visit Mexican

156
00:06:51,502 --> 00:06:54,724
Mafia members in prison, hold money, and pass

157
00:06:54,724 --> 00:06:55,369
messages.

158
00:06:55,819 --> 00:06:59,409
In June 2019, the system comes out in a new

159
00:06:59,409 --> 00:07:02,581
federal case against Rancho San Pedro.

160
00:07:03,031 --> 00:07:05,977
14 members and associates are charged.

161
00:07:05,977 --> 00:07:09,464
Prosecutors allege they sold methamphetamine,

162
00:07:09,464 --> 00:07:13,030
heroin, cocaine and opioids out of a hotel and

163
00:07:13,030 --> 00:07:16,130
two bars on Pacific Avenue in San Pedro.

164
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:19,286
The taxes, they say, went to three Mexican

165
00:07:19,286 --> 00:07:21,798
Mafia members serving long state prison

166
00:07:21,798 --> 00:07:23,151
sentences for murder.

167
00:07:23,601 --> 00:07:26,723
On the morning the indictments are unsealed,

168
00:07:26,723 --> 00:07:29,348
four federal defendants are arrested.

169
00:07:29,348 --> 00:07:31,831
Seven are already in state custody.

170
00:07:31,831 --> 00:07:33,250
Three are fugitives.

171
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:36,443
10 more people are arrested on local charges.

172
00:07:36,893 --> 00:07:39,530
Prosecutors said wiretapped conversations

173
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:42,296
linked members to murders, attacks on rival

174
00:07:42,296 --> 00:07:45,190
gang members, and the discipline of their own

175
00:07:45,190 --> 00:07:45,640
people.

176
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:48,795
The lead defendant is Robert Messersmith,

177
00:07:48,795 --> 00:07:49,917
known as Stretch.

178
00:07:49,917 --> 00:07:52,885
Prosecutors said he ran the gang's day-to-day

179
00:07:52,885 --> 00:07:55,590
operations, and reported to Mexican Mafia

180
00:07:55,590 --> 00:07:56,778
members in prison.

181
00:07:57,228 --> 00:08:00,944
Between August 2017 and May 2018, according to

182
00:08:00,944 --> 00:08:04,175
prosecutors, he sold dozens of oxycodone

183
00:08:04,175 --> 00:08:07,568
pills, arranged heroin and methamphetamine

184
00:08:07,568 --> 00:08:11,607
deals, and planned to smuggle drugs into a prison.

185
00:08:12,057 --> 00:08:15,155
On a recorded call in May 2018, he talked

186
00:08:15,155 --> 00:08:17,347
about a successful drug deal.

187
00:08:17,797 --> 00:08:21,404
He pleaded guilty to a drug conspiracy charge.

188
00:08:21,404 --> 00:08:25,011
In January 2021, a federal judge sentenced him

189
00:08:25,011 --> 00:08:26,736
to 10 years in prison.

190
00:08:27,736 --> 00:08:30,496
Six years after that indictment, the warrants

191
00:08:30,496 --> 00:08:31,171
come again.

192
00:08:31,621 --> 00:08:35,589
Early on October 7, 2025, teams serve 17

193
00:08:35,589 --> 00:08:39,855
locations in San Pedro and the harbor area.

194
00:08:40,305 --> 00:08:43,645
This time it's the FBI, the LAPD, Homeland

195
00:08:43,645 --> 00:08:47,065
Security Investigations, and the California

196
00:08:47,065 --> 00:08:48,814
Department of Justice.

197
00:08:48,814 --> 00:08:52,313
FBI SWAT teams come in from Los Angeles, Las

198
00:08:52,313 --> 00:08:55,812
Vegas, Phoenix and San Diego, along with the

199
00:08:55,812 --> 00:08:58,119
Bureau's Hostage Rescue Team.

200
00:08:58,569 --> 00:09:01,609
14 people are named in a federal complaint.

201
00:09:01,609 --> 00:09:04,297
Thirteen are charged with racketeering

202
00:09:04,297 --> 00:09:07,974
conspiracy, and with conspiring to distribute drugs.

203
00:09:07,974 --> 00:09:10,025
Five more face state charges.

204
00:09:10,475 --> 00:09:13,817
According to the FBI, some members give orders

205
00:09:13,817 --> 00:09:17,014
